    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d148-a46">

                <pb facs="0440" n="318" sameAs="frus:frus1889/pg318"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure G 4.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Consulate</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Apia</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1882-04-01"><hi
                                rendition="#italic">April</hi> 1, 1882</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#small-caps">August Godefroy</hi>, Esq.:</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your letter of yesterday with a complaint against Mr. A. Nelson, of Safune,
                    “selling arms and ammunition against the order of prohibition issued by the
                    Government, &amp;c.”</p>
                <p>I have to inform you that Mr. Nelson will appear at this consulate on Monday, May
                    15, 1882, to answer your complaint. I have to request that you will have the
                    witnesses mentioned in your letter here on that date, to substantiate the
                    charge.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer><signed>J. E. VARICK ALVORD,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Acting United
                            States Vice-Consul.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
